// Coh+rlx -- Coh (Coh.lit) over relaxed accesses.
//
// Source: Arlt & Vafeiadis, "RGSep under Release/Acquire Consistency",
//         PACMPL 10 (OOPSLA2), Article 375, 2026. doi:10.1145/3839507, Section 3, which states this outcome is possible under the relaxed
// fragment of C11 and under SCOH. herd7 and MoRDor both forbid it under RC11
// and Coherence: see Coh.lit.
//
// Reference verdicts:
//   herd7 7.58 on herd/Coh+rlx.litmus, under the zoo's abstract-sc, abstract-tso,
//     ra, sra, wra and abstract-coherence cat models and herd's rc11.cat:
//     WRA allows; SC, TSO, RA, SRA, Coherence and RC11 forbid.
// The paper's registers are renamed a -> ra, b -> rb:
// MoRDor reads only names beginning with r as registers.
x := 0; y := 0; z := 0;
{ x.store(1, rlx); ra := x.load(rlx); y.store(ra, rlx) }
||| { x.store(2, rlx); rb := x.load(rlx); z.store(rb, rlx) }
%%
allow (ra = 2 && rb = 1) [WRA]
forbid (ra = 2 && rb = 1) [SC, TSO, RA, SRA, Coherence, RC11]
